{number: 59}
{title: Rescue the Perishing}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Rescue the perishing, [Eb] care for the dying,
[Bb] Snatch them in pity from [F7] sin and the grave;
[Bb] Weep o’er the erring one, [Eb] lift up the fallen,
[Bb] Tell them of Jesus the [F7] mighty to [Bb] save.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Rescue the [F7] perishing,
Care for the [Bb] dying;
[Eb] Jesus is [Bb] merciful,
[F7] Jesus will [Bb] save.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] Tho’ they are slighting Him, [Eb] still He is waiting,
[Bb] Waiting the penitent [F7] child to receive;
[Bb] Plead with them earnestly, [Eb] plead with them gently,
[Bb] He will forgive if they [F7] only be-[Bb] lieve.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Bb] Down in the human heart, [Eb] crushed by the tempter,
[Bb] Feelings lie buried that [F7] grace can restore;
[Bb] Touched by a loving heart, [Eb] wakened by kindness,
[Bb] Chords that were broken will [F7] vibrate once [Bb] more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Bb] Rescue the perishing, [Eb] duty demands it;
[Bb] Strength for thy labor the [F7] Lord will provide;
[Bb] Back to the narrow way [Eb] patiently win them;
[Bb] Tell the poor wanderer a [F7] Saviour has [Bb] died.
{end_of_verse}
